1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,000
On a night of heavy rain, a giant tunnel wakes up under Yangcheon-gu, Seoul.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,700
This area floods often. Streets used to go under water whenever it rained.

3
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:14,550
So they dug a tunnel 10 m wide, 40 m underground.

4
00:00:14,550 --> 00:00:18,600
It's about 4.7 km long, and much wider than a subway tunnel.

5
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:23,150
Just before rainwater overflows, it pours down a shaft into the tunnel.

6
00:00:23,150 --> 00:00:27,200
This tunnel can hold up to 320,000 tons of rainwater.

7
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:31,400
When the rain stops, pumps slowly push the water out to the Han River.

8
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:36,600
While we sleep, a giant water bowl under the city keeps our town safe.
